1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,967
Beachcar. Your Codex. Your taste. Your car.

2
00:00:05,967 --> 00:00:08,560
I live in a tiny beach town.

3
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:15,303
All summer, I'm running my kids one or two miles at a time—to the beach, camp, friends, ice cream.

4
00:00:15,303 --> 00:00:20,521
I wanted a beach car: open, simple, weird, and unlike anything else in town.

5
00:00:20,671 --> 00:00:23,087
But I didn't know what it was called.

6
00:00:23,087 --> 00:00:24,995
I didn't even know it existed.

7
00:00:24,995 --> 00:00:28,684
Most car sites make you name the answer before they'll help you search.

8
00:00:28,684 --> 00:00:31,355
So I built Beachcar to start with the feeling.

9
00:00:31,505 --> 00:00:36,257
I tell it what I like, and my Codex goes hunting from my Mac.

10
00:00:36,257 --> 00:00:41,099
It opens the browser I'm already signed into, digs through listings, throws away the noise,

11
00:00:41,099 --> 00:00:43,610
and comes back with a few actual opinions:

12
00:00:43,610 --> 00:00:47,884
this one fits, this one's overpriced, this one could ruin my summer.

13
00:00:48,034 --> 00:00:52,612
For a couple of weeks, I kept using it and teaching it:

14
00:00:52,612 --> 00:00:55,258
more charm, less precious; more beach day, less car show.

15
00:00:55,258 --> 00:01:00,845
Then this appeared—a 1960 Willys Surrey that looks like a Jeep, a golf cart,

16
00:01:00,845 --> 00:01:02,963
and a beach umbrella somehow became one car.

17
00:01:02,963 --> 00:01:04,618
I bought it.

18
00:01:04,618 --> 00:01:07,521
This is actually my car now.

19
00:01:07,671 --> 00:01:11,971
GPT-5.6 gives Codex the judgment to do that hunt,

20
00:01:11,971 --> 00:01:17,435
and Codex helped me build Beachcar too—the iPhone experience, the way it searches, even this film.

21
00:01:17,435 --> 00:01:23,079
If you opt in, your Codex can also take a weekly Garage Session to improve Beachcar itself.

22
00:01:23,079 --> 00:01:25,020
You see every change first.

23
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:26,662
Nothing ships without you.

24
00:01:26,812 --> 00:01:30,534
I built Beachcar to find one weird little car for my family.

25
00:01:30,534 --> 00:01:33,154
Now your Codex can go looking for yours.

26
00:01:33,154 --> 00:01:36,739
Beachcar. Your Codex. Your taste. Your car.
